From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:25:15 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Windows 10 Mobile: V8's JIT under W^X

A UWP app gets executable memory only through VirtualAllocFromApp and
VirtualProtectFromApp, never writable and executable at once. Pages V8
asks to be read-write-execute are made read-execute and recorded; a
vectored exception handler flips the faulting page to read-write on a
write and back to read-execute (flushing the instruction cache) when it
runs. Both in PartitionAlloc (V8's pages in Chromium, through gin) and
in V8's own platform code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../page_allocator_internals_win.h            | 216 ++++++++++++++++++
 v8/src/base/platform/platform-win32.cc        | 201 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 417 insertions(+)

